Qt Advanced Docking System (QtADS) 5.1.1
Upstream: https://github.com/githubuser0xFFFF/Qt-Advanced-Docking-System
Tag v5.1.1, commit 023ce95934fecfd4cf5c672c9c404fabe0f54923
License: LGPL-2.1-or-later (LICENSE, gnu-lgpl-v2.1.md, unchanged)

Retained: src/*.cpp, src/*.h and src/linux/ unchanged except three patches; cmake/modules/ads_version.h.in
as ads_version.h.in. Not retained: images/ and stylesheets/; ads.qrc is replaced
by an empty resource of the same name, which DockManager still initializes. CMRemote sets
CDockManager::DisableStylesheet and styles the docks from app/ui/theme.qss; dock
buttons use app-drawn icons registered with the ADS icon provider.
CMakeLists.txt here is CMRemote's own static build, not upstream's.

CMRemote patch (src/DockAreaWidget.cpp, CDockAreaLayout, marked "CMRemote patch"):
upstream detaches a dock area's inactive tabs with setParent(nullptr), so every tab
switch moved a session's GPU-backed view (QRhiWidget) out of its window and back.
Inactive tabs now stay hidden children of their area; a removed tab keeps its parent
until it is inserted into another area.

CMRemote patch (src/DockAreaTabBar.cpp onTabWidgetMoved, src/DockWidgetTab.cpp moveTab,
src/DockAreaWidget.cpp reorderDockWidget, marked "CMRemote patch"): upstream reorders a
dragged tab only on mouse release, so the other tabs stay put while it slides over them.
The tab now emits moved() on every drag step; once the cursor passes a neighbour's centre,
the tab bar and dock area reorder immediately and the neighbours slide aside. The area moves
the tab in its list without hiding or re-showing the current session view.

CMRemote patch (src/DockWidgetTab.cpp rejoinTabBar, marked "CMRemote patch"): upstream
keeps a tab pulled out of its bar as a floating preview until the mouse is released, even
when it is brought back over a tab bar. Now, while the preview is over the tab bar of a
dock area holding tabs of the same kind (CMRemote's "session" tab property), the preview
is dropped, the dock widget joins that area at the cursor (if it is another area), and
the drag continues as an ordinary tab move.
